# NOTE: tauri.conf.json / package.json / vite.config.js / .gitignore must NOT
# be ignored here, even as a "just in case" safeguard. They are tracked, so git
# ignores the patterns — but gitignore-aware tooling (globby with gitignore:
# true, which tauri-action@v1 uses to locate src-tauri/tauri.conf.json) filters
# purely by pattern and fails with "Couldn't detect Tauri dir".

# ── Compliance / legal files must ALWAYS be tracked ───────────────────────────
# The blanket *.md / *.txt / *.lock rules above would silently drop these.
# Keep the negations below in sync with anything added for store submission or
# license compliance (verified with: git check-ignore -v <path>).
!README.md
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!SECURITY.md
!PRIVACY.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!SUPPORT.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!NOTICE.txt
!docs/**/*.md
!src-tauri/Cargo.lock
!pnpm-lock.yaml

# ── Python tooling (scripts/generate-notices.py) ────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
